SADIE HRTF database (https://github.com/resonance-audio/resonance-audio, commit 4556a46afd4ffae092aa281bfd072eb0279d3a29)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In quench_audio: the head-related impulse responses of its HRTF (src/audio/HrtfTable.inc, written by
tools/make_hrtf_table.py from third_party/SADIE_hrtf_database/WAV/Subject_002/DFC/48K_24bit in the archive of that
commit). The measurements are the SADIE project's (University
of York; Subject 002 is a Neumann KU100 dummy head; http://www.york.ac.uk/sadie-project/binaural.html), as
Resonance Audio distributes them. Changed: reduced to 386 of the 1555 directions, the onsets cut off and kept as
delays, truncated to 128 taps with a fade, rescaled and quantized to 16 bits (stated in the file's header). The
folder's LICENSE is the Apache License 2.0, without a copyright line; there is no NOTICE file:

